course: dictionary
lesson: 9132
title: Snail and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. A snail is a small, slow animal with a soft, slimy body and a spiral shell on its back. It can live on land or in water. «Snails have a ribbon-shaped tongue covered in thousands of tiny teeth» is a fact about the animal itself.
explain: The word snail also describes speed. When we say something happens «at a snail's pace», we mean it is very slow. The context tells you which meaning is right: is the sentence about a creature, or about how fast something moves?
explain: Phrases can change a word's meaning. «Snail mail» means letters sent by post, not a snail carrying a letter. «A snail shell» is the shell that a snail carries on its back. Check the words around snail to find out which meaning fits.
fact: A snail is a small, slow animal with a soft, slimy body.
fact: A snail has a spiral shell on its back and can live on land or in water.
fact: «At a snail's pace» means very slowly.
fact: «Snail mail» means letters sent by post.
fact: Snails are molluscs, and gardeners often see them as pests because they eat plants.
exercise: «Snails have a ribbon-shaped tongue covered in thousands of tiny teeth that wear down and are replaced.» What is covered in thousands of tiny teeth? | The shell | The foot | *The tongue | The slime
exercise: «Zoos breed rare small animals like Partula snails, nearly wiped out on their islands by one predator snail that people brought in.» Why were the Partula snails nearly wiped out? | They were too fast to catch | *A predator snail that people brought in | People kept too many as pets | Floods washed them away
exercise: «A snail is a living creature; killing animals for fun is unkind.» What does this sentence say a snail is? | *A living creature | A kind of stone | A machine | A plant with leaves
test: Lily waited at a snail's pace for the bus to arrive. What does "at a snail's pace" mean? | *Very slowly | Very fast | Very dark | Very loudly
test: Grandma still sends birthday cards by snail mail. What does "snail mail" mean? | A snail shell sold in a shop | Mail carried by a snail | Email sent very quickly | *Letters sent by post
exam: Which fact about snails is true? | Snails never eat plants | *Snails have a shell on their back | Snails fly through the air | Snails have eight legs
